Brief: Tell me how MangoDB's indexes work and when a query uses them. — about IndexData

1. export interface IndexData {
2. /** For equality lookups: Map<serializedKeyValue, Set<documentIdString>> */
3. equalityMap: Map<string, Set<string>>;
4. /** For range queries: sorted array of { value, docIds } for single-field indexes */
5. sortedEntries: Array<{ value: unknown; docIds: Set<string> }>;
6. /** The first field in the index (used for range queries) */
7. firstField: string;
8. /** Reference to the index metadata */
9. indexInfo: IndexInfo;

Which sentence is most worth keeping for the brief? Reply {"sentence": "<number>"} or {"sentence": "none"}.
